# 🧪 Test Case Structure Guidelines

When **creating or editing** test cases, follow the required structure. Full criteria, keyword lists, and examples are in the **validate-test-cases** skill.

## Required sections (brief)

| Section | Required |
|--------|----------|
| **Summary** | User Story, Product, Brand, Account type(s) — all mandatory |
| **Preconditions** | Entry points required; Note optional |
| **Steps** | At least one; active voice, precise verbs; no vague statements |
| **Keywords** | Min. one product type, one brand, one platform (Web/Mobile); no "automated"/"automatable" |
| **Test Type** | One of: `end2end`, `BDD`, `Integration`, `UI_Automation` |
| **Attachments** | Required if SAF account creation in preconditions (.json) |
| **Linked Requirements / Related Issues** | At least one requirement or related issue linked (в TestIT — секция "Related Issues") |

**For full checklists and allowed keywords** → use the **validate-test-cases** skill (`.cursor/skills/validate-test-cases/reference.md`).

**To validate a test case and get a report** → ask to "validate this test case" or "check test case structure"; the agent will use the validate-test-cases skill and return the structured report.

**Canonical JSON payload and HTML templates** for draft/TestIT: `.cursor/rules/test-case-payload-format.mdc`.
